T* (over the old ground which was, and is, to us so full of vivid and) Tj
T* (terrible memories. It was almost impossible to believe that the things) Tj
T* (which we had seen with our own eyes and heard with our own ears were) Tj
T* (living truths. Every trace of all that had been was blotted out. The) Tj
T* (castle stood as before, reared high above a waste of desolation.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (When we got home we were talking of the old time--which we could all) Tj
T* (look back on without despair, for Godalming and Seward are both happily) Tj
T* (married. I took the papers from the safe where they had been ever since) Tj
T* (our return so long ago. We were struck with the fact, that in all the) Tj
T* (mass of material of which the record is composed, there is hardly one) Tj
T* (authentic document; nothing but a mass of typewriting, except the later) Tj
T* (note-books of Mina and Seward and myself, and Van Helsing?s memorandum.) Tj
T* (We could hardly ask any one, even did we wish to, to accept these as) Tj
T* (proofs of so wild a story. Van Helsing summed it all up as he said, with) Tj
T* (our boy on his knee:--) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (?We want no proofs; we ask none to believe us! This boy will some day) Tj
T* (know what a brave and gallant woman his mother is. Already he knows her) Tj
T* (sweetness and loving care; later on he will understand how some men so) Tj
T* (loved her, that they did dare much for her sake.?) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (JONATHAN HARKER.) Tj
